; An amount that lies exactly halfway between two figures at its
; commodity's display precision prints rounded half away from zero
; (format_mpq_exact in src/amount.cc), whatever the binary expansion of
; the value.  At precision 1 the postings print A 0.25 as 0.3, B 0.35 as
; 0.4, C 0.45 as 0.5, D 0.15 as 0.2, F 0.55 as 0.6, G 0.65 as 0.7 and
; H 0.75 as 0.8 in the rows below.  E's 0.05 is exactly half a unit,
; which amount_t::is_zero counts as zero, so E has no row although the
; amount by itself would print as 0.1; --unround shows it.  The semantic
; bisimulation (test/semantic/check_all.py) replays this journal, so an
; oracle that rounds a tie any other way, or that gives the 0.05 tie a
; row, fails here.

2015/01/01 ties
    A   (0.5 * 0.5 FOO)
    B   (0.5 * 0.7 FOO)
    C   (0.5 * 0.9 FOO)
    D   (0.5 * 0.3 FOO)
    E   (0.5 * 0.1 FOO)
    F   (0.5 * 1.1 FOO)
    G   (0.5 * 1.3 FOO)
    H   (0.5 * 1.5 FOO)
    Z

test bal
             0.3 FOO  A
             0.4 FOO  B
             0.5 FOO  C
             0.2 FOO  D
             0.6 FOO  F
             0.7 FOO  G
             0.8 FOO  H
            -3.2 FOO  Z
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal E --unround
            0.05 FOO  E
end test
